<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">3 June in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">8 events that happened on 3 June, from 713 to 1989.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/byzantine-empire" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/byzantine-empire.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">713 CE <span class="tih-ago">1,313 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Byzantine emperor Philippicus is blinded and deposed</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Soldiers sent by George Buraphus, count of the Opsician army, seized and blinded Emperor Philippicus, who had taken power in a coup against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/justinian-ii">Justinian II</a> in 711. He was succeeded by Anastasios II.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/byzantine-empire">Byzantine Empire</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1602">1602 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">424 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The English navy defeats a Spanish fleet at Sesimbra Bay</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">In the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anglo-spanish-war-1585-1604">Anglo-Spanish War</a>, an English force under Richard Leveson and William Monson met Spanish <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/galley">galleys</a> and a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carrack">carrack</a> at Sesimbra Bay in Portugal, sinking two galleys and capturing the carrack. It was the last expedition Queen <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/elizabeth-i">Elizabeth I</a> sent to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anglo-spanish-war-1585-1604">Anglo-Spanish War</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carrack">Carrack</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1621">1621 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">405 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Dutch West India Company receives its charter</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The States General granted the company a trade monopoly in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/americas">Americas</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/west-africa">West Africa</a>. It founded New Netherland, seized part of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brazil">Brazil</a> and became a major Atlantic slave trader.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/dutch-empire">Dutch Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch-west-india-company">Dutch West India Company</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brazil">Brazil</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1839">1839 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">187 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Lin Zexu begins destroying confiscated opium at Humen</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The Chinese commissioner had over a thousand tonnes of British-traded opium mixed with lime and salt and flushed into the sea. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a>'s response led to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-opium-war">First Opium War</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/qing-empire">Qing Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-opium-war">First Opium War</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1940">1940 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">86 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Luftwaffe bombs Paris</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">In Operation Paula, German aircraft struck airfields and factories around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a>, killing some 250 people. Eleven days later German troops entered the city.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1942">1942 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">84 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Battle of Midway opens with US air attacks</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Bombers from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-midway">Midway</a> Atoll attacked the approaching Japanese invasion force. The next day US carrier aircraft sank four Japanese carriers, turning the tide of the Pacific war.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/empire-of-japan">Empire of Japan</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-midway">Battle of Midway</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1989">1989 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">37 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Chinese troops move on Tiananmen Square</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">On the night of 3 to 4 June, the army forced its way into central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/beijing">Beijing</a>, firing on crowds. Hundreds, possibly thousands, were killed, ending seven weeks of pro-democracy protest.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/beijing">Beijing</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1989">1989 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">37 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Ayatollah Khomeini dies in Tehran</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ruhollah-khomeini">Ruhollah Khomeini</a>, leader of the 1979 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iranian-revolution">Iranian Revolution</a> and the Islamic Republic's first Supreme Leader, died aged 86. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ali-khamenei">Ali Khamenei</a> succeeded him the next day.</p></div></li></ol>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-born"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-born">Born on 3 June <span class="n">7</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/bogislaw-x"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/bogislaw-x.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Bogislaw X</span><span class="tp">1454–1523</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/charles-ii-archduke-of-austria"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/charles-ii-archduke-of-austria.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Charles II, Archduke of Austria</span><span class="tp">1540–1590</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/manuel-belgrano"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/manuel-belgrano.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Manuel Belgrano</span><span class="tp">1770–1820</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/jefferson-davis"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/jefferson-davis.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Jefferson Davis</span><span class="tp">1808–1889</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/louis-faidherbe"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/louis-faidherbe.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Louis Faidherbe</span><span class="tp">1818–1889</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/george-v"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/george-v.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">George V</span><span class="tp">1865–1936</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/raul-castro"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/raul-castro.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Raúl Castro</span><span class="tp">b. 1931</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-died"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-died">Died on 3 June <span class="n">5</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/guaimar-iv-of-salerno"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/guaimar-iv-of-salerno.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Guaimar IV of Salerno</span><span class="tp">c. 1013–1052</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/thomas-hutchinson-governor"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/thomas-hutchinson-governor.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Thomas Hutchinson (governor)</span><span class="tp">1711–1780</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/mikhail-kalinin"><span class="ph ph-person" aria-hidden="true"></span><span><span class="nm">Mikhail Kalinin</span><span class="tp">1875–1946</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/hjalmar-schacht"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/hjalmar-schacht.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Hjalmar Schacht</span><span class="tp">1877–1970</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/ruhollah-khomeini"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/ruhollah-khomeini.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Ruhollah Khomeini</span><span class="tp">1902–1989</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<p class="day-ppl-note">Dates as the sources give them: in the Julian calendar before 1582, and in some countries for longer (Britain until 1752, Russia until 1918). Only people whose day of birth or death the records agree on are listed.</p>
